/-!
# CORE2A, design pass 14: assembly of `Thm26bTorusProp`

This file assembles Bender 1981 p. 220 (the second half of Theorem 2.6, the "torus" crux of
`Thm26bOneClass`) from the leaves of `Submission/Work/_design_gw/Core14.lean`:

* `Work.CORE2A.c14_T1` (`R^y ≤ O(Ĥ)`),
* `Work.CORE2A.c14_R_struct` (the structure of `R_u = [t, C_E(u)]` for `u ∈ S ∖ E`),
* `Work.CORE2A.c14_k` (`kE B = kTor q`),
* `Work.CORE2A.c14_four_dvd` (`4 ∣ |⟨t, R, R*⟩|`),

together with the elementary leaves `c14_W1`, `c14_W2`, `c14_arith`, `c14_mul_mem_layer`,
`c14_S_normalizes`.

Given `t ∈ E(Ĥ)`, `|S| ≥ 8` and an involution `s ∈ S ∖ E(Ĥ)`, we produce
`y ∈ N_G(⟨t,s⟩)` with `y t y⁻¹ = s` and `4 ∣ |E(Ĥ) ∩ Ĥ^y|`.  The construction is Bender's:
`g ∈ N_G(V)` with `g(ts)g⁻¹ = t` (`c14_W2`), `w ∈ S` with `w s w⁻¹ = ts` (`c14_W1`),
`y := g⁻¹ w g`.  The group `X* := R*^g` is centralized by `E` (`c14_T1`), hence normalized by
`S` (`c14_S_normalizes`), which gives `y R* y⁻¹ = R*`; finally
`⟨t, R_s, R_{ts}⟩ ≤ E ∩ Ĥ^y` and `4 ∣ |⟨t, R_s, R_{ts}⟩|` (`c14_four_dvd`).
-/

